    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "An eighteenth-century mechanical duck that swallowed corn and grain and, after a pregnant pause, relieved itself of an authentic-looking burden was the improbable forebear of modern technologies designed to simulate animal and intelligent processes. Quaint as the Duck now seems, we remain in an age that it inaugurated; its mixed career set in motion a dynamic that has characterized the subsequent history of artificial life.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Riskin, J. (2023). The Defecating Duck, Or, The Ambiguous Origins of Artificial Life. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/zb803xz9154. https://doi.org/10.25740/zb803xz9154.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
